{"content":[{"signature":"","thinking":"\nThe task is DATA-HDB-01, which involves computing a Minimum Spanning Tree (MST) using mutual reachability distances (HDBSCAN-style). Let me analyze what's needed:\n\n1. The input has `nodes`, `core_distance` (per node), and `distances` (pairwise distances)\n2. The mutual reachability distance between two points u, v is: `max(core_distance[u], core_distance[v], distance(u,v))`\n3. We need to build an MST on these mutual reachability distances\n4. Return the MST edges as `[node1, node2, weight]` and the `total_weight`\n\nLet me implement Kruskal's or Prim's algorithm for this.\n\nFor the MST:\n- Compute mutual reachability distance for each edge: `mrd(u,v) = max(core_dist[u], core_dist[v], dist(u,v))`\n- Run Kruskal's algorithm on these edges\n- Return edges sorted by weight (or in the order they were added)\n\nLet me write the solve function:\n\n```python\ndef solve(case):\n    nodes = case[\"nodes\"]\n    core_distance = case[\"core_distance\"]\n    distances = case[\"distances\"]\n    \n    # Compute mutual reachability distances\n    mrd_edges = []\n    for u, v, d in distances:\n        mrd = max(core_distance[u], core_distance[v], d)\n        mrd_edges.append((mrd, u, v))\n    \n    # Sort by mutual reachability distance\n    mrd_edges.sort()\n    \n    # Kruskal's MST with Union-Find\n    parent = {node: node for node in nodes}\n    rank = {node: 0 for node in nodes}\n    \n    def find(x):\n        while parent[x] != x:\n            parent[x] = parent[parent[x]]\n            x = parent[x]\n        return x\n    \n    def union(x, y):\n        rx, ry = find(x), find(y)\n        if rx == ry:\n            return False\n        if rank[rx] \u003c rank[ry]:\n            rx, ry = ry, rx\n        parent[ry] = rx\n        if rank[rx] == rank[ry]:\n            rank[rx] += 1\n        return True\n    \n    mst_edges = []\n    total_weight = 0.0\n    \n    for mrd, u, v in mrd_edges:\n        if union(u, v):\n            mst_edges.append([u, v, mrd])\n            total_weight += mrd\n    \n    return {\n        \"mst_edges\": mst_edges,\n        \"total_weight\": total_weight\n    }\n```\n\nLet me verify with the first fixture:\n- nodes: p0, p1, p2, p3, p4\n- core_distances: p0=0.23243377, p1=0.50398147, p2=0.55673811, p3=0.66828478, p4=0.43968915\n\nDistances and MRDs:\n- p0-p1: max(0.23243377, 0.50398147, 0.89672724) = 0.89672724\n- p0-p2: max(0.23243377, 0.55673811, 0.73968893) = 0.73968893\n- p0-p3: max(0.23243377, 0.66828478, 0.77270596) = 0.77270596\n- p0-p4: max(0.23243377, 0.43968915, 0.87376631) = 0.87376631\n- p1-p2: max(0.50398147, 0.55673811, 1.08418122) = 1.08418122\n- p1-p3: max(0.50398147, 0.66828478, 0.82719237) = 0.82719237\n- p1-p4: max(0.50398147, 0.43968915, 0.61293041) = 0.61293041\n- p2-p3: max(0.55673811, 0.66828478, 1.00286271) = 1.00286271\n- p2-p4: max(0.55673811, 0.43968915, 0.5322912) = 0.55673811\n- p3-p4: max(0.66828478, 0.43968915, 0.51351834) = 0.66828478\n\nSorted MRD edges:\n1. p2-p4: 0.55673811\n2. p3-p4: 0.66828478\n3. p1-p4: 0.61293041... wait let me re-sort\n\nActually:\n- p2-p4: 0.55673811\n- p1-p4: 0.61293041\n- p3-p4: 0.66828478\n- p0-p2: 0.73968893\n- p0-p3: 0.77270596\n- p1-p3: 0.82719237\n- p0-p4: 0.87376631\n- p0-p1: 0.89672724\n- p2-p3: 1.00286271\n- p1-p2: 1.08418122\n\nKruskal's:\n1. p2-p4 (0.55673811) → add, components: {p2,p4}, {p0}, {p1}, {p3}\n2. p1-p4 (0.61293041) → p1 and p4 in different components → add, components: {p1,p2,p4}, {p0}, {p3}\n3. p3-p4 (0.66828478) → p3 and p4 in different components → add, components: {p1,p2,p3,p4}, {p0}\n4. p0-p2 (0.73968893) → p0 and p2 in different components → add, components: {p0,p1,p2,p3,p4}\nMST complete!\n\ntotal_weight = 0.55673811 + 0.61293041 + 0.66828478 + 0.73968893 = 2.57764223\n\nThe implementation looks correct. Let me format this as the required JSON response.\n","type":"thinking"},{"text":"{\"implementation\": \"def solve(case):\\n    nodes = case[\\\"nodes\\\"]\\n    core_distance = case[\\\"core_distance\\\"]\\n    distances = case[\\\"distances\\\"]\\n\\n    # Compute mutual reachability distance for each edge\\n    # mrd(u, v) = max(core_distance[u], core_distance[v], dist(u, v))\\n    mrd_edges = []\\n    for u, v, d in distances:\\n        mrd = max(core_distance[u], core_distance[v], d)\\n        mrd_edges.append((mrd, u, v))\\n\\n    # Sort edges by mutual reachability distance for Kruskal's algorithm\\n    mrd_edges.sort()\\n\\n    # Union-Find data structure\\n    parent = {node: node for node in nodes}\\n    rank = {node: 0 for node in nodes}\\n\\n    def find(x):\\n        while parent[x] != x:\\n            parent[x] = parent[parent[x]]  # path compression\\n            x = parent[x]\\n        return x\\n\\n    def union(x, y):\\n        rx, ry = find(x), find(y)\\n        if rx == ry:\\n            return False\\n        if rank[rx] \u003c rank[ry]:\\n            rx, ry = ry, rx\\n        parent[ry] = rx\\n        if rank[rx] == rank[ry]:\\n            rank[rx] += 1\\n        return True\\n\\n    # Kruskal's MST\\n    mst_edges = []\\n    total_weight = 0.0\\n\\n    for mrd, u, v in mrd_edges:\\n        if union(u, v):\\n            mst_edges.append([u, v, mrd])\\n            total_weight += mrd\\n            if len(mst_edges) == len(nodes) - 1:\\n                break\\n\\n    return {\\n        \\\"mst_edges\\\": mst_edges,\\n        \\\"total_weight\\\": total_weight\\n    }\\n\"}","type":"text"}],"id":"msg_01hkRSL2LunAacaIi7MqqZ3d","model":"claude-opus-4-7","role":"assistant","stop_reason":"end_turn","stop_sequence":null,"type":"message","usage":{"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":2121},"cache_creation_input_tokens":2121,"cache_read_input_tokens":0,"inference_geo":"not_available","input_tokens":16,"output_tokens":2049,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":1562},"service_tier":"standard"}}